# CODEOWNERS — the mechanism behind RULE-01 and RULE-09.
#
# Since ADR-004 unwired guard-registry.mjs, this file is what makes "the registry is human-only" true
# of a pull request. It moved the control from before the write to before the merge; it did not
# remove it. Deleting a line here removes a control, and nothing else will report that it is gone.
#
# Owner stamped by scripts/init-project.mjs.
#
# TODO(project): branch protection requiring CODEOWNERS review is a GitHub repository setting and no
# script can turn it on. Until it is on, this file is documentation rather than a control, RULE-01
# has no mechanism, and the enforcement map in .ai/registry/rules.md is claiming something untrue.

/.ai/registry/    @didi-code0980
/.ai/standards/   @didi-code0980
/.claude/         @didi-code0980
/.github/         @didi-code0980
/scripts/         @didi-code0980
/.mcp.json        @didi-code0980

# `scripts/` was added on 2026-09-06, with `OWED_PATHS` in `scripts/check-docs.mjs`. That register
# tells check D6 that a named-but-absent path is owed rather than broken, which is a waiver on the
# audit — and a waiver an agent can grant itself to clear its own gate is not a control. The rest of
# the directory earns the same review for the same reason: `check-docs.mjs` and `check-allowed-paths.mjs`
# ARE the audit, and `.claude/hooks/**` has been behind owner review since this file was written.

